    {
      "id": "b413c466-8239-4787-94f3-b1623d041aad",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 301,
      "shortId": "72FCK",
      "priority": 14,
      "shortName": "overlay-follow-ups-anchor-to-r",
      "title": "Overlay follow-ups: anchor-to-rect mode + convert Select/Tooltip/ContextMenu/CommandPalette panels; overlay sizing + scrollable modal body; SDF glyph glow",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Follow-up scope deferred out of T009 (base Overlay + BUG A, d448702) and T011 (rest glow, 7ff3b59).\n\n⚠️ SCOPE SPLIT 2026-07-24 — two chunks moved to their own tasks:\n- **F003/P011/T015** — Overlay sizing (.panel_size) + scrollable modal body. **DONE 2026-07-24.**\n- **F003/P011/T016** — SDF glyph/text glow renderer (Icon + RailCell rest glow). Renderer work.\n\nSTEPS 1–4 (placement authority, Select, docs, ContextMenu/CommandPalette + the FrameStyle setting) are COMMITTED + USER-VERIFIED — see the detail retained below.\n\n═══ STEP 5 — TOOLTIP: DECIDED + BUILT 2026-07-25, AWAITING VISUAL VERIFICATION ═══\n\n**USER DECISION (2026-07-25): unify BOTH chrome and placement.** I recommended leaving the Tooltip alone (a tooltip is not a panel; a `place_beside` authority would have exactly one caller — YAGNI) and flagged the risk. The user chose full unification. Their call; implemented in full rather than half-done.\n\nWHAT WAS BUILT (uncommitted — pending the user's eyes on the GPU showcase):\n1. **`place_beside(anchor, panel, viewport, gap, side) -> Rectangle`** in `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/overlay.rs` — the THIRD placement authority, beside `place_anchored_on` (rect, leading-edge aligned, below↔above) and `place_at_point` (point, corner-offset, down-right↔up-left). `place_beside` is the rect + **centered cross-axis** + all-four-sides rule. They are three functions, not one with flags, because they differ in ALIGNMENT — documented as a table in the rustdoc and in docs/widgets.md.\n2. **`BesideSide { Top | Bottom | Left | Right }`** — no `Auto` variant, deliberately: \"beside\" has no natural default direction the way a dropdown has \"below\". Private `opposite()` + `fits()` helpers on the enum.\n3. **`TooltipSide` is now `pub type TooltipSide = BesideSide;`** — a true alias, not a second enum, so the two can never disagree about what `Top` means. All 5 external call sites (showcase ×3, heca/src/chrome/mod.rs, heca/src/providers/workspaces.rs, tests) compile unchanged.\n4. **`Tooltip::fits` + the body of `bubble_rect` DELETED** (~40 lines) → `bubble_rect` is now a one-line delegation to `place_beside`.\n5. **Tooltip paints through `paint_panel_chrome`** — so `[appearance] overlay_border_style` (none|bordered|bracketed) governs the tooltip edge like every other panel. The tooltip supplies only its identity: accent edge colour (`interaction.tooltip_border`) + a tighter/fainter halo (`BUBBLE_GLOW_RADIUS 5.0`, `BUBBLE_GLOW_INTENSITY 0.2`, named consts).\n\nDELIBERATE NON-CHANGE — **main axis is NOT clamped.** Only the cross axis clamps, matching the tooltip's previous behaviour exactly. Clamping the main axis would slide the bubble OVER the target it describes. When neither side fits, the preferred side is kept and the panel overflows. Locked by `beside_keeps_the_preferred_side_when_neither_fits`. (`place_anchored_on` DOES clamp its main axis — the two rules differ on purpose.)\n\nPURITY INVARIANT RE-PROVEN (the T014 STEP 2 bug, for the 4-side case): `place_beside`'s result DOES depend on the viewport (both the flip and the clamp read it). That is safe here **only because the tooltip bubble places no child components** — its text is a `cx.text` draw, not a laid-out child, so there is no layout-vs-paint disagreement to have. Written as a \"purity note\" section in the rustdoc and as a ⚠️ callout in docs/widgets.md: draw-only, or don't use it.\n\nTESTS (+5 unit, +1 doctest; workspace 868 → 874 green, clippy clean):\n`beside_centers_on_the_cross_axis`, `beside_flips_to_the_opposite_side_when_there_is_no_room` (all four sides), `beside_clamps_only_the_cross_axis`, `beside_keeps_the_preferred_side_when_neither_fits`, `beside_infinite_viewport_keeps_the_preferred_side_unclamped`.\n\nDOCS (both audiences, per the grid-ui rule): rustdoc on `place_beside`/`BesideSide`/`TooltipSide`/`bubble_rect` + module doc; `docs/widgets.md` §Tooltip rewritten (placement + surface now delegated, the ViewNode \"host-only\" note added) and §Overlay's \"which authority to call\" table gained the `place_beside` row + the three-authority alignment comparison + the purity ⚠️.\n\nSHOWCASE: new four-side demo row (TOP/BOTTOM/LEFT/RIGHT buttons) under \"IconButton · Tooltip\", so the flip and the OVERLAY FRAME restyle are both drivable.\n\n⚠️ **VISUAL RISK TO CHECK — this is why it is not committed.** `paint_panel_chrome` replaces the bubble's old `control_radius().min(h/2)` with the panel `border_radius`, and adds the panel drop shadow (`SHADOW_DROP 16`, blur ×6) + the bracket reticle under `Bracketed`. On a small hover bubble that shadow/reticle may read as far too heavy — exactly the concern raised before the decision. If it does, the options are (a) revert to the tooltip's own chrome, (b) give `PanelChrome` a shadow/radius scale, or (c) accept it. Do not commit until the user has driven `cargo run -p heca-renderer --example showcase`.\n\n═══ RETAINED — STEPS 1–4 DETAIL ═══\nSTEP 1 (COMMITTED da5961d, USER-VERIFIED): `place_anchored` + `place_at_point` + `OverlayPosition{Center|Anchored}` + `.position()`/`.anchored()`/`.set_anchor()`; ContextMenu::layout delegates to `place_at_point`.\nSTEP 2 (COMMITTED d14c24d, USER-VERIFIED \"now looks good\"): Select `panel_top()` removed → `place_anchored_on`; NEW `AnchorSide{Auto|Below|Above}` (load-bearing: Select computes flip + visible-row COUNT together); NEW `paint_panel_chrome` + `PanelChrome`. Select rows stay PLACED CHILDREN (`bounds === drawn === clickable`), which is why Select paints its own panel.\n⚠️ STEP 2 BUG (fixed): an interim version clamped Select's panel to the viewport cached at paint. `panel_rect()` is computed TWICE per frame (layout `place_options()` + `paint()`), so a time-varying input makes them disagree and rows DETACH. Fix: `panel_rect()` is PURE (infinite viewport passed deliberately); on-screen fit comes from capping visible row COUNT in `open_list()`. Guards: `open_panel_rect_is_independent_of_the_cached_viewport`, `flipped_panel_is_not_clamped_even_when_it_overflows_the_top`.\nSTEP 3 (COMMITTED 742cf5f, 98fd6a5): docs/widgets.md §Overlay \"Implementing an overlay-panel widget\" — path A (compose an Overlay), path B (paint it yourself, reuse the authorities), the ⚠️ pure-rect invariant, the authority table.\nSTEP 4 (COMMITTED fa4dab8, 1260226, 0388296, 5913787, USER-VERIFIED \"to me it look ok now\"): context_menu.rs + command_palette.rs → `paint_panel_chrome`. ALL FOUR panels share one chrome; `FrameStyle::` matched in exactly ONE place. NEW `FrameStyle{None|Bordered|Bracketed}` + `colors.overlay_frame` in heca-theme (grid-ui reads it at paint, can't depend on heca-config — same path as `show_focus_border`); `[appearance] overlay_border_style` in heca-config; applied in `chrome_gui_theme` ⇒ live-reloads. Showcase got an OVERLAY FRAME select (it builds its own Theme, never reads config.toml). SHADOW raised on user feedback: BLUR_MULT 4→6, DROP 12→16. ⚠️ BUG (0388296): `overlay_frame` governed only the RETICLE while `chrome.border` drew unconditionally ⇒ None left the accent border on screen. Now it owns the WHOLE edge; `PanelChrome.border` = the widget's preferred edge COLOUR, ignored under None; fill+glow never suppressed. Also fixed a PRE-EXISTING red test: `GlowLevel::Thin.strength_scale()` was 0.75 in code but asserted 0.5.\n\n═══ REMAINING IN T014 ═══\n- User drives the showcase and confirms the tooltip bubble. Then commit and close.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\n═══ CLOSED 2026-07-25 — all five steps delivered + user-verified ═══\n\nSTEP 5 (Tooltip) is now done and confirmed. User verdict on the first build: \"the shadow is too much I think. everything else looks correct\" — placement, flip, frame styles and glow all approved on sight; only the shadow depth was wrong. After the elevation fix: \"now the shadow is ok\".\n\nWHAT SHIPPED IN STEP 5:\n1. `place_beside(anchor, panel, viewport, gap, side)` — the THIRD placement authority in `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/overlay.rs`. Rect anchor + CENTERED cross axis + all four sides, vs `place_anchored_on` (leading-edge aligned, below↔above) and `place_at_point` (corner-offset, down-right↔up-left). Three functions, not one with flags, because they differ in ALIGNMENT — comparison table in the rustdoc and in docs/widgets.md.\n2. `BesideSide { Top | Bottom | Left | Right }` — no `Auto` variant on purpose (\"beside\" has no natural default direction the way a dropdown has \"below\"). Private `opposite()` + `fits()` helpers.\n3. `TooltipSide` is now `pub type TooltipSide = BesideSide` — a true alias, so there is ONE four-sided vocabulary. All 5 external call sites compile unchanged.\n4. `Tooltip::fits` + the body of `bubble_rect` deleted (~40 lines) → one-line delegation.\n5. Tooltip paints via `paint_panel_chrome`, so `[appearance] overlay_border_style` governs it like every other panel.\n6. **`PanelElevation { Panel | Hover }` on `PanelChrome`** — added in response to the user's shadow feedback. The panel shadow (blur 48, drop 16) is tuned for surfaces hundreds of px across; on a ~30px bubble it was LARGER THAN THE BUBBLE. `Hover` = `HOVER_SHADOW_SCALE` (0.25) → blur 12, drop 4. Blur and drop scale TOGETHER so the shadow keeps its shape and only loses depth. Deliberately a semantic variant, NOT a raw shadow override: a caller names a depth, the painter owns the pixels (AGENTS.md — no hand-calculated styling at call sites). The field was added WITHOUT `..Default::default()` at the three panel sites, so the compiler forced Select/ContextMenu/CommandPalette to each declare `PanelElevation::Panel` — a future overlay widget cannot silently inherit the wrong depth.\n\nDELIBERATE NON-CHANGE — main axis is NOT clamped by `place_beside` (only the cross axis), matching the tooltip's previous behaviour. Clamping it would slide the bubble OVER the target it describes. Locked by `beside_keeps_the_preferred_side_when_neither_fits`. Note `place_anchored_on` DOES clamp its main axis — the rules differ on purpose.\n\nPURITY INVARIANT RE-PROVEN for the 4-side case: `place_beside`'s result DOES depend on the viewport (flip + clamp both read it), which the T014-STEP-2 invariant forbids for a rect that positions children. Safe here ONLY because the tooltip bubble places no child components (its text is a `cx.text` draw). Documented as a \"purity note\" in the rustdoc and a ⚠️ callout in docs/widgets.md: draw-only, or don't use it.\n\nSHADOW IS NOT PART OF THE FRAME POLICY — `overlay_frame: none` removes the edge but never the shadow (depth ≠ edge). Locked by `hover_elevation_leaves_the_edge_policy_untouched`.\n\nTESTS — workspace 868 → 881 green, clippy clean under `--all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`:\nplacement — `beside_top_centers_the_panel_horizontally_on_the_anchor`, `beside_left_centers_the_panel_vertically_on_the_anchor`, `beside_top_flips_below_when_the_anchor_hugs_the_viewport_top`, `beside_bottom_flips_above_…`, `beside_left_flips_right_…`, `beside_right_flips_left_…`, `beside_clamps_only_the_cross_axis`, `beside_keeps_the_preferred_side_when_neither_fits`, `beside_infinite_viewport_keeps_the_preferred_side_unclamped`;\nelevation — `hover_elevation_casts_a_shallower_shadow_than_a_panel`, `hover_elevation_scales_blur_and_drop_together` (asserts the RATIO, so retuning a constant can't silently distort the shape), `hover_elevation_leaves_the_edge_policy_untouched`;\nplus a `place_beside` doctest.\n\nRUST REVIEW (mandated pre-commit, run against the rust-best-practices handbook) — two findings found and fixed before commit:\n(a) Ch 1.7 imports — I had `use super::overlay::…`; every sibling widget uses `crate::widgets::…` alphabetically with functions before types. Fixed. (Note: the repo's own order is `crate::*` → `heca_core` → `std`, which is NOT the handbook's canonical order; AGENTS.md forbids `cargo fmt`, so matching the file wins.)\n(b) Ch 5.1/5.4 one behaviour per test — a 4-assert flip test and a 2-loop centering test were split into 6 single-assertion tests over a shared `beside_at()` fixture (`rstest` is not a dependency here). Two tests keep 2 assertions where the claim is \"X changes, Y doesn't\" and a single assert cannot express the \"only\"; both carry actual-vs-expected failure messages.\nConsidered deviation: `place_beside` takes `Rectangle` (32 bytes) by value, over the handbook's ~24-byte guideline — kept, because `Rectangle` is `Copy` throughout and both sibling authorities have exactly this signature.\n\nDOCS (both audiences): rustdoc on `place_beside` / `BesideSide` / `PanelElevation` / `TooltipSide` / `bubble_rect` + the tooltip module doc; docs/widgets.md §Tooltip rewritten, §Overlay gained the `place_beside` row in the authority table, the three-authority alignment comparison, the purity ⚠️, and a `PanelElevation` table.\n\nSHOWCASE: new TOP/BOTTOM/LEFT/RIGHT tooltip row under \"IconButton · Tooltip\" — makes the four-side flip and the OVERLAY FRAME restyle drivable.\n\n═══ RETAINED — STEPS 1–4 DETAIL ═══\nSTEP 1 (COMMITTED da5961d, USER-VERIFIED): `place_anchored` + `place_at_point` + `OverlayPosition{Center|Anchored}` + `.position()`/`.anchored()`/`.set_anchor()`; ContextMenu::layout delegates to `place_at_point`.\nSTEP 2 (COMMITTED d14c24d, USER-VERIFIED \"now looks good\"): Select `panel_top()` removed → `place_anchored_on`; NEW `AnchorSide{Auto|Below|Above}` (load-bearing: Select computes flip + visible-row COUNT together); NEW `paint_panel_chrome` + `PanelChrome`. Select rows stay PLACED CHILDREN (`bounds === drawn === clickable`), which is why Select paints its own panel.\n⚠️ STEP 2 BUG (fixed): an interim version clamped Select's panel to the viewport cached at paint. `panel_rect()` is computed TWICE per frame (layout `place_options()` + `paint()`), so a time-varying input makes them disagree and rows DETACH. Fix: `panel_rect()` is PURE (infinite viewport passed deliberately); on-screen fit comes from capping visible row COUNT in `open_list()`. Guards: `open_panel_rect_is_independent_of_the_cached_viewport`, `flipped_panel_is_not_clamped_even_when_it_overflows_the_top`.\nSTEP 3 (COMMITTED 742cf5f, 98fd6a5): docs/widgets.md §Overlay \"Implementing an overlay-panel widget\" — path A (compose an Overlay), path B (paint it yourself, reuse the authorities), the ⚠️ pure-rect invariant, the authority table.\nSTEP 4 (COMMITTED fa4dab8, 1260226, 0388296, 5913787, USER-VERIFIED \"to me it look ok now\"): context_menu.rs + command_palette.rs → `paint_panel_chrome`. ALL FOUR panels share one chrome; `FrameStyle::` matched in exactly ONE place. NEW `FrameStyle{None|Bordered|Bracketed}` + `colors.overlay_frame` in heca-theme (grid-ui reads it at paint, can't depend on heca-config — same path as `show_focus_border`); `[appearance] overlay_border_style` in heca-config; applied in `chrome_gui_theme` ⇒ live-reloads. Showcase got an OVERLAY FRAME select. SHADOW raised on user feedback: BLUR_MULT 4→6, DROP 12→16 — which is exactly what later made the unscaled shadow wrong on a tooltip, hence `PanelElevation`. ⚠️ BUG (0388296): `overlay_frame` governed only the RETICLE while `chrome.border` drew unconditionally ⇒ None left the accent border on screen. Now it owns the WHOLE edge. Also fixed a PRE-EXISTING red test: `GlowLevel::Thin.strength_scale()` was 0.75 in code but asserted 0.5.\n\nFOLLOW-UPS SPUN OUT: F003/P011/T015 (overlay sizing — DONE), F003/P011/T016 (SDF glyph glow — next, technique decided: additive halo pass), F004/P001/T008 (unify scrollbars).",
