      "completedAt": "2026-07-24T21:52:20.964Z",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-24T17:25:26.669Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-24T21:52:20.964Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "33f9e6f5-3f69-4849-8bc0-e4cccb111877",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 303,
      "shortId": "KBL4B",
      "priority": 16,
      "shortName": "sdf-glyph-text-glow-renderer-i",
      "title": "SDF glyph/text glow renderer — Icon + RailCell rest glow",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Split out of T014 (2026-07-24). USER-REQUESTED follow-up to T011 (rest glow, 7ff3b59 + 319a349). RENDERER work.\n\nTHE GAP: T011 gave every bordered SURFACE a faint rest glow, but a GLYPH could not carry one — `TextCmd` had no glow field and glow lived only in the SDF rect renderer.\n\n═══ TECHNIQUE — DECIDED BY USER 2026-07-25: (a) ADDITIVE HALO PASS ═══\nOptions presented were (a) additive halo pass, (b) true SDF text atlas, (c) offscreen bloom. User chose (a). Rejected for now: (b) is a multi-session change that puts the TERMINAL glyph path (the hottest in the app) at risk; (c) duplicates F004/P002/T001 \"Implement offscreen bloom pipeline\", which is a real but unstarted task — building it here would have been the wrong task id.\n\nFACTS VERIFIED IN CODE BEFORE BUILDING (the task's 2026-07-17 line numbers were stale):\n- Glyph atlas is R8Unorm COVERAGE with `PAD: u32 = 1` (atlas.rs:17) ⇒ a multi-tap blur READ in the fragment shader would bleed into neighbouring atlas entries. That is why the halo is offset COPIES, not a shader blur.\n- Text pipeline uses `PREMULTIPLIED_ALPHA_BLENDING` (text.rs) and the fragment returned `(rgb*a, a)` ⇒ emitting `a == 0` with `rgb > 0` is exactly additive — the same trick grid.wgsl:146 uses for rect glow. This is what makes the halo read as light rather than as a grey smear.\n- `Icon::paint` already stacked TWO glyph layers, so a halo layer is a third, not a new mechanism.\n\n═══ BUILT 2026-07-25 — UNCOMMITTED, AWAITING GPU VERIFICATION ═══\nARCHITECTURE: the SCENE asks for a glow DECLARATIVELY (`TextCmd.glow: Option<Glow>`, mirroring `RectCmd.glow`); the RENDERER decides how to realize it. Swapping the multi-tap for a true SDF pass later changes no widget and no scene code.\n\nheca-grid-ui:\n- `scene.rs` — `TextCmd.glow: Option<Glow>`.\n- `component.rs` — `PaintCx::icon_glowing(rect, glyph, color, size, glow)`; `icon()` delegates with `None`. Applies `scaled_glow` INTERNALLY, so the glyph halo goes through the ONE chokepoint (no second glow scale).\n- `component.rs` — `PaintCx::with_content_glow(Option<Glow>, f)` + `content_glow()`. The halo counterpart of `with_content_color`, added for the same reason: a control holds children as `impl Component` and cannot style them, so it PUBLISHES and the glyph PULLS.\n- `widgets/icon.rs` — `Icon::glow(bool)` (default false). Opt-in, NOT automatic: most icons sit inside an already-glowing control, so haloing all of them would double the light. Resolution order mirrors colour: own opt-in → inherited content glow → flat. Only the PRIMARY layer haloes (haloing the secondary wash too would double the light on every duotone glyph for a second set of taps). `HALO_RADIUS = 6.0` (tighter than a surface's — a glyph's strokes are thin, a wide halo reads as a smudge).\n- `widgets/rail_cell.rs` — publishes `rest_glow(ICON_HALO_RADIUS)` for its subtree ONLY at rest (hover/active/disabled already have lit chrome). This is the \"RailCell bare-icon rest glow\" the task asked for, achieved without RailCell reaching into its child.\n\nheca-renderer:\n- `text.rs` — `TextGlow { color, radius, intensity }` + `TextGlow::is_visible()` (the SINGLE definition of \"inert\", used by both emission and cache hashing). `TextCommand.glow`; `queue_text_in_box` gained the parameter (its only caller is scene.rs). `queue_text` / `queue_text_in_line_box_with_style` pass None. `queue_terminal_run` hard-codes None with the reason in a comment.\n- `text.rs` — `TextVertex.additive: f32` + `shader_location: 3` on BOTH pipelines. `EmitKey.glow_bits` (halo quads are baked into cached vertices, so a glow change must miss the cache).\n- `text.rs` — emission rewritten: a `push_quad` closure (kills the 4x vertex duplication), `HALO_TAPS = 8` copies on a ring of `radius * HALO_OFFSET_FRAC (0.35)`, per-tap alpha = `color.a * intensity / HALO_TAPS` so the taps SUM BACK to the requested strength instead of blowing out 8x. Halo emitted BEFORE the sharp glyphs. **The ink bbox is grown by the ring reach** — otherwise damage/clip culling would scissor away the very light the halo adds outside the glyph box (the task's damage-model edge case).\n- `text.wgsl` — `additive` through vertex→fragment; `out_a = a * (1.0 - additive)`.\n- `scene.rs` — maps `TextCmd.glow` → `TextGlow`.\n\nBUG FOUND BY MY OWN TEST: `glow_bits` hashed the raw colour even for an INERT glow (alpha 0 / radius 0), so two commands producing identical output (no halo) got different cache keys and would rebuild geometry every frame. Also the \"is it visible\" predicate was DUPLICATED between emission and hashing and could drift. Fixed by extracting `TextGlow::is_visible()` and filtering through it in both places.\n\nTESTS (+6; workspace 881 → 887 green, clippy clean under `--all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`):\ngrid-ui `widgets::icon::tests::glow::` — `an_icon_is_flat_by_default`, `opting_in_carries_a_halo_on_the_glyph_run`, `glow_size_none_removes_the_glyph_halo` (THE chokepoint guard), `glow_size_scales_the_glyph_halo`.\nrenderer — `emit_key_distinguishes_the_glow`, `emit_key_treats_a_transparent_glow_as_no_glow` (the bug above).\n\nDOCS (both audiences): rustdoc on `TextCmd.glow`, `PaintCx::icon_glowing`, `with_content_glow`/`content_glow`, `Icon::glow`, `TextGlow`/`is_visible`, `TextVertex.additive`, `HALO_TAPS`/`HALO_OFFSET_FRAC`, `ICON_HALO_RADIUS`. docs/widgets.md: §Icon gained the halo bullet-set + a runnable example + a note on why `glow` is NOT a ViewNode prop; the §\"glow model — who owns what\" line that said **\"Icons/glyphs cannot glow yet\"** is now CORRECTED and explains the technique + why the atlas forces offset copies.\n\nSHOWCASE: new \"Icon — glyph halo\" section — FLAT vs GLOW side by side (accent + foreground), so the GLOW SIZE select visibly scales it and `none` removes it.\n\n═══ REMAINING ═══\n1. USER VERIFICATION in `cargo run -p heca-renderer --example showcase` — fully GPU-gated, unit tests cannot confirm a halo. Check: (a) the FLAT vs GLOW pair actually differs; (b) GLOW SIZE none/thin/medium/large scales it and none kills it; (c) the halo reads as light, not as a grey smudge or a drop shadow (if it looks smudgy, lower `HALO_OFFSET_FRAC`; if banded/lumpy, raise `HALO_TAPS`); (d) no visible perf change scrolling the showcase or in the terminal (terminal glyphs must be untouched).\n2. Then commit.\n3. NOT DONE / OPEN: nothing in the app opts in yet — `Icon::glow` is available and `RailCell` publishes at rest, but no app-side chrome sets it. Decide with the user whether any real chrome icon should light up.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\n═══ CLOSED 2026-07-25 — delivered + user-verified (\"now its fine\") ═══\n\nTECHNIQUE — the user first chose (a) an additive multi-tap halo. That was BUILT, then ABANDONED after visual verification, and replaced with a **blurred glyph in the atlas** (also user-approved). Recording why, so nobody rebuilds the discarded one:\n\n**Why the ring of copies failed** (4 rounds of GPU verification): a ring is a DISCRETE shell, so the copies read as spokes and arcs, never as light. It also degraded as the radius grew — a fixed tap count spreads thinner, and at `glow_size = large` the copies became a countable lattice. Deriving the tap count from ring circumference fixed the lattice but not the shells. Two rings, 12–46 taps, four tuning constants — still structurally wrong. **Do not reintroduce it.**\n\n═══ WHAT SHIPPED ═══\n`Atlas::glyph_blurred(.., sigma)` rasterizes the glyph's coverage mask, pads by 3σ, blurs (three box passes ≈ Gaussian), **renormalizes the peak back to full coverage**, and stores it as its own atlas entry keyed by `(glyph, sigma bucket)`. Emission draws ONE quad per glyph sampling it.\n- 24–92 quads/glyph → **1**. Continuous falloff by construction. σ scales with `glow_size` for free.\n- `Atlas::clear()` drops the blurred cache too (its UVs would otherwise dangle).\n- `PlacedGlyph` carries its `CacheKey` — the layout is cached independently of any glow, so the blurred variant can only be resolved at emission.\n\nheca-grid-ui: `TextCmd.glow` (declarative, mirroring `RectCmd.glow` — the renderer decides how to realize it); `PaintCx::icon_glowing` (applies `scaled_glow` internally = the ONE chokepoint); `PaintCx::with_content_glow`/`content_glow` (halo counterpart of `with_content_color`: a control holds children as `impl Component` and cannot style them, so it publishes and the glyph pulls); `Icon::glow(bool)` opt-in; `RailCell` publishes at rest only.\nheca-renderer: `TextGlow` + `is_visible()`; `TextVertex.additive` + `shader_location: 3` on both pipelines; `EmitKey.glow_bits` + `glow_mode_bits`; `text.wgsl` `out_a = a * (1.0 - additive)`; `TextRenderer::set_glow_alpha_scale` wired from `enqueue_scene`.\n\n═══ THREE BUGS FOUND DURING VERIFICATION ═══\n1. **Halo invisible at first (ring era).** Per-tap alpha was `intensity / HALO_TAPS` on the theory that taps \"sum back\". They sit on a ring and barely overlap, so each contributed 1.5% alpha. Wrong reasoning, not a typo.\n2. **Halo vanished entirely on switching to the blur.** Blurring conserves energy, NOT peak: spreading a thin stroke over σ≈4px drops its peak to ~¼, so the halo came out at ~0.03 alpha. FIX: renormalize the blurred mask to full peak — which also makes `intensity` mean *peak alpha*, the same quantity a rect's glow peaks at, so the two are comparable instead of eyeballed. Locked by `a_blurred_mask_is_renormalized_back_to_full_peak`.\n3. **Light theme absent.** `grid.wgsl` switches rect glow to a translucent tinted halo on light backgrounds (`glow_alpha_scale`) because ADDING light to a near-white surface does nothing. `enqueue_scene` already computed it; the text path ignored it. The glyph path now mirrors the rect's own curve (`sqrt(base) * glow_alpha_scale`) rather than a linear scale.\nPlus a doc bug: `with_content_glow` claimed the published glow was pre-scaled. It is not — `rest_glow()` returns unscaled and the chokepoint scales once; the doc would have led to double-scaling.\n\n═══ CALIBRATION — the load-bearing insight ═══\nMatching a lit surface means matching **emitted light**, not peak alpha. Perceived glow scales with the emitting PERIMETER: a glyph's is ~¼ of a button's, so identical peak + identical radius still looks dimmer and tighter (user: \"do you see the icon button glow the same as the Top/Bottom/Left/Right buttons?\" — no). Final values sit deliberately ABOVE parity, and each constant's rustdoc says so, so they are not \"corrected\" back later:\n- `HALO_RADIUS_FRAC = 0.55` of glyph size (34px glyph → 18.7px reach; Button's rest glow is 12.0). Derived from glyph size, not fixed — a 20px toolbar icon must not get the same absolute halo as a 34px one.\n- `HALO_DARK_GAIN = 1.6` (peak 0.189), `HALO_LIGHT_GAIN = 1.6` (peak 0.341). Moved together so the themes cannot drift.\n\n═══ VERIFICATION ═══\n803 tests green in the crates touched (heca-grid-ui/heca-renderer/heca/heca-config/heca-theme), 0 failures; clippy clean under `--all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`.\nNEW: `atlas::tests::` — `a_blurred_mask_is_renormalized_back_to_full_peak` (bug 2), `..._is_padded_for_the_blur_to_spread_into`, `..._reports_its_padded_dimensions`, `..._falls_off_with_distance`, `a_wider_sigma_pads_further`. `widgets::icon::tests::glow::` — flat by default, opt-in carries a halo, `glow_size=none` removes it (THE chokepoint guard), `glow_size` scales it. renderer — `emit_key_distinguishes_the_glow`, `emit_key_treats_a_transparent_glow_as_no_glow`.\n`blur_mask` was extracted as a PURE function precisely so bug 2 is caught by a test instead of by the user's eyes — four rounds of visual verification were spent on things a test could have caught.\n\n⚠️ UNRELATED PRE-EXISTING FLAKE (not caused by this work, not fixed here): `heca-core`'s PTY tests (`terminal_backend_*`) fail ~2 runs in 6 with \"shell output should include echoed marker\" after a ~30s timeout, a different one each time. Verified by stashing ALL changes and reproducing on the committed baseline; `heca-core` has no dependency on the crates touched here. **Worth its own task.**\n\n═══ DOCS ═══\nrustdoc on every new item incl. WHY each constant sits where it does. docs/widgets.md: §Icon halo bullets + runnable example + why `glow` is not a ViewNode prop; §\"the glow model\" corrected — the line \"Icons/glyphs cannot glow yet\" was false and now describes the blur, with an explicit \"do not reintroduce the ring of copies\" note.\nSHOWCASE: \"Icon — glyph halo\" section, FLAT vs GLOW side by side.\n\n═══ OPEN (deliberately not done) ═══\nNothing in the app opts in yet: `Icon::glow` exists and `RailCell` publishes at rest, but no real chrome icon is lit. That is a design call for the user.",
      "notes": "",
