    {
      "id": "7d82f8e0-a7cc-4922-b96b-667207c2be4e",
      "phaseId": "4d4aa26b-6245-4c0f-8bdf-64573a7afbf5",
      "number": 307,
      "shortId": "PT33R",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "separate-layout-settings-from",
      "title": "Separate layout settings from visual settings in Style (make the plugin boundary a type)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "PREREQUISITE for T2. Do this first — T2's whole-struct merge is unsafe until it lands.\n\nCURRENT STATE\n`heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs:211` — one flat `Style` struct, `#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]`\n(style.rs:210), embedded in `Base` on every widget. It mixes two categories:\n- LAYOUT (plugin-writable): direction, justify, align, align_self, justify_items, justify_self, gap,\n  margin + per-side overrides, padding + padding_x/padding_y, pad_spacing_x/y, gap_spacing, width,\n  height, min_width, min_height, max_width, max_height, flex_grow, flex_shrink, hidden, grid_cell.\n- VISUAL (host/theme-owned, NEVER plugin-writable): fill, border, glow, accent, fg, radius,\n  font_size, font_scale, size, size_explicit (style.rs:289-315).\n\nWHY\n\"Styling is not a property — the plugin picks intent, the host resolves the pixels from the Theme\"\nis rule C of docs/chrome-and-ui.md §2.6.1 and appears in AGENTS.md's SETTLED table\n(\"Is styling a prop? NO\"). T2 merges a node's properties straight into the layout settings; if the\ntwo categories stay in one struct, that merge hands plugins raw colours and borders. The boundary\nmust be enforced by the type system, not by whoever reviews the next PR.\n\nBORDERLINE — decide explicitly and record the reasoning in the task:\n- `size` / `size_explicit` / `font_scale` are SEMANTIC (Small/Normal/Big), already exposed as the\n  `size` property and legitimately plugin-writable. They are visual by category but allowed by rule.\n  Suggest a third group, or an allow-marker on the visual side. Do NOT silently lump them in.\n- `hidden` and `grid_cell` are layout, not visual, despite sitting near the visual block.\n\nWORK\n- Group the fields. Preferred: nested `Style { layout: Layout, visual: Visual, .. }`. `Style` is\n  `Copy` and flat today and is touched by every widget plus the layout pass, so a nested split is a\n  wide mechanical change — measure it before committing to the shape. A flat struct with a derive\n  marker per field is the fallback if nesting proves too invasive.\n- Keep every existing call site compiling. `LayoutExt`/`StyleExt` (heca-grid-ui/src/builders.rs)\n  write through `base_mut().style` and must keep working unchanged — this is a data reorganisation,\n  not an API change.\n- `StyleExt` is deliberately NOT implemented for `Flex` (builders.rs:1-10) so a layout-only\n  container cannot become a styled surface. Preserve that.\n\nBEHAVIOUR TO PRESERVE\nEverything visual. This task must produce ZERO rendering change. Per AGENTS.md, green tests are not\nverification for anything visual — build the showcase and have the user look before closing.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n- Layout and visual fields are separately addressable as types.\n- Full workspace green, clippy clean under --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings.\n- No visual diff in the showcase (user-verified).\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-25 — commit 8718718 on branch feat/p017-t1-style-split. User verified in the showcase: no visual change.\n\nSHAPE SHIPPED (differs from the \"preferred\" one in the original description — the user chose it):\n    pub struct Style { pub layout: Layout, pub visual: Visual }\nTwo PEERS, neither privileged. Not `Style { ...layout fields flat..., visual: Visual }`, which was\nbuilt first and then redone: that version needed `#[serde(skip)]` on the visual field for T2, i.e.\nONE line whose deletion would silently make colours plugin-writable. The peer shape needs no serde\nattribute at all — `Layout` will derive serialization in T2, `Visual` simply will not. style.rs now\ncontains ZERO serde attributes. That is the whole point: nothing to forget, and the default outcome\nis correct on both sides.\n\nFIELD ASSIGNMENT + REASONING\n- `Layout` (caller-owned, will be serializable): direction, justify, align, align_self,\n  justify_items, justify_self, gap, gap_spacing, margin + 4 per-side overrides, padding,\n  padding_x/y, pad_spacing_x/y, width, height, min/max width+height, flex_grow, flex_shrink,\n  hidden, grid_cell, size, size_explicit.\n- `Visual` (theme-owned, never serializable): fill, border, glow, radius, font_size, font_scale.\n- `size`/`size_explicit` → Layout: SEMANTIC (Small/Normal/Big), not a pixel value, and the layout\n  pass reads it and cascades it to children. `set_size` moved to Layout.\n- `font_scale` → Visual: a RAW multiplier. The semantic route a description may take is `size`.\n- `to_taffy()` / `to_taffy_grid()` moved onto `Layout` — they read only those fields.\n\nDEAD CODE REMOVED: `Style::accent` and `Style::fg`. Declared with hardcoded colour literals in the\nDefault impl (Color::rgb(137,180,250) / (205,214,244)) and never read or written anywhere in the\nworkspace — widgets go through `theme.colors.accent`. Compiler-confirmed unused.\n\nMEASUREMENT (for T2 and anyone sizing similar work): 52 files, ~200 layout accesses, ~25 visual.\nA grep for `.style.<field>` UNDERCOUNTS badly — many sites reach fields through a `&Style` binding\n(`let s = &mut base.style; s.padding_x = ..`). Those were fixed by rebinding to `.style.layout`,\nwhich left the block bodies untouched. Use `cargo build --workspace --all-targets` to enumerate:\nplain `--workspace` skips examples and tests, and heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs plus\nheca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs both needed the rewrite.\n\nNEW EXPORTS: `Layout` and `Visual` alongside `Style` from the heca-grid-ui crate root (lib.rs:64).\n\nVERIFICATION: 899 tests pass, 0 failures. clippy --all-targets --all-features --locked -D warnings\nexits 0 (only the pre-existing `block v0.1.6` future-incompat note). Builder API unchanged —\n`.gap()`, `.fill()`, `.font_size()` behave exactly as before; LayoutExt/StyleExt write to the\ncorrect half internally, and StyleExt is still NOT implemented for Flex.\n\nDOCS: docs/widgets.md §`Style` & layout enums rewritten for the pair, including why `size` is on\none side and `font_scale` the other, and stating that builder calls did not change.",
      "notes": "",
